column56:
Interesting.  Even in Perl we cache and garbage-collect anon classes.<p>(The caching is for the very common case of creating a subclass with optional roles applied:<p><pre><code>    my $class = Some::Meta::Class->create_anon_class(
        superclasses => ['Foo'],
        roles        => [qw/Commonly Applied Traits/],
    );
</code></pre>
There is almost no speed hit the second time you create an instance of "Foo" with "Commonly", "Applied", and "Traits" applied.  Not sure this would be useful for Java, although we can achieve the same effect as in the article.)
